  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">YAL - Ishimwe - Iriba Clean Water</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Water/Services .Beneficiaries: YALI Youth 803 of which 402 are women ..2 volunteer staff, 1 intern/trainee, 200 households will gain access to clean water (avg. household - 4 x 200 = 800) ...The grant will be used to pump underground water in form of boreholes. Then the water will be treated and purified to safe drinking standards for usage in household activities. After the production and purification process, the treated clean water will be delivered to peoples homes in all possible means via bicycles, delivering truck, and pipes dependent on what a customer prefers to use and can afford. ..The grant funds will be used to: (a) drill an additional borehole; (b) the purchase of a water storage tank; and (c) the construction of a piping system directly connected to the water storage tank. .</narrative>
  </description>
